INTERPRETATION: the walk succeeds only when NO component is a symlink. On macOS `/tmp` and `/var` are OS-provided symlinks into `/private`, and `$TMPDIR` is always under `/var/folders/...`, so every path the platform's own temp APIs hand out is refused by an O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY walk. Linux has no such top-level symlinks, which is why this never appeared there.
